  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "History",
      "items": [
        "Unit state is a pure fold over the append-only execution history; nothing is stored",
        "Any in-flight condition accepts launch_uncertain, suspended, cancellation_requested, capture unmonitored and terminated; only the common paths are drawn",
        "Outcomes: completed, failed, backtracked, interrupted",
        "Inactivity alone proves neither failure nor closure; only loss of the host event stream marks watched executions and open activities unmonitored"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Assurance",
      "items": [
        "Assurance is recorded apart from outcome on the unit's current attempt: verified, failed, blocked, impossible or unverified",
        "A completed finish whose attempt has no evaluated result is recorded in the same batch as unverified, never as accepted work",
        "A result applies only to its own attempt and changes no lifecycle fact; evidence for an earlier revision stays historical",
        "The snapshot and TUI carry assurance separately from state, flight and outcome"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Session events, no unit state",
      "items": [
        "denied, contest_requested, recovery_declared, recovery_closed, actions_observed, actions_uncertain, restoration_confirmed, stop_declared, escalation_requested, user_exception",
        "They change budgets or recovery accounting only; a denial consumes nothing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Budgets",
      "items": [
        "Specialists 4, unplanned units 4, contests 3, consecutive recovery failures 2",
        "Each declared recovery: at most 200 actions and 3 attempts",
        "A user exception adds allowance beside consumption"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Interlocutor",
      "items": [
        "A lent interface is switched, handed off or aborted; one holder at a time",
        "Resume is conduct in the prompt; the code has no resume verb"
      ]
    }
  ]
}